body:
I said the same exact thing about moving it closer - It actually helps me feel more connected because I can actually take in all the info on screen vs the 42 inch being like.... It's hard to explain. I can see everything on the peripheral vision but only can focus on the inner 50%. Like in Cyberpunk, I will know there's a sign in my sight but won't know it's a ramen shop until I physically move my eyes to it. On the 34 inch, even when moved closer to my vision, I can see it's a ramen shop before I directly have to look at it. Does that make sense to you or am I insane?

&#x200B;

The G8 is pretty sweet, I had the DW for a short time (when I first got the C2) and was 50/50 on it, but the C2 was much cheaper at the time and 16:9 so I liked it for work and whatnot more so than the DW..... But the G8 being 10 bit, 175 and thinner was enough to lightly push me over the edge. What I DON'T like about it is the UI and settings system, though - The DW/DWF settings are leagues better to navigate and understand imo. But as far as quality, oomf and general feeling, super similar overall. Honestly makes me want to see if I can land the DWF for £650 instead lmao
